<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT - NatWest's 15 Euro stocks for 1997.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - NatWest's 15 Euro stocks for 1997.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Strategists at NatWest Securities on Tuesday named 15 European stocks they expect to outperform during 1997.</p>
<p>The list included French insurer Axa, Swiss chemicals group Clariant, Swiss bank group CS Holding, now known as Credit Suisse Group, Dutch chemicals group DSM, Swedish bank Svenska Handelsbanken, Dutch window coverings maker Hunter Douglas, French luxury goods group LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton, Finnish telecoms group Nokia Oy and Spanish petrochemical group Repsol.</p>
<p>Also named were Swiss pharmaceuticals group Roche Holding, German packaging producer Schmalbach-Lubeca AG, Italian state-owned telecommunications group Stet, French oil company Total SA, Germany's diversified utility group Viag AG and Dutch publisher NV Verenigd Bezit VNU.</p>
<p>NatWest strategists said in a strategy research note covering Europe excluding the UK that &quot;the outlook for European equity markets in 1997 is bright.&quot;</p>
<p>Switzerland, France, Italy and Spain were picked out as the favoured markets.</p>
<p>&quot;Valuations against bonds and cash are highly supportive, protecting from any major fall-out should the U.S. market come under pressure.&quot;</p>
<p>NatWest said the Euro-15 stock selection focuses on &quot;the major theme of management action to improve returns,&quot; and tempers &quot;our long-held favour for growth equities.&quot;</p>
<p>--Elaine Hardcastle, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
